        "category": "offensive",
        "deathNote": false,
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature fails to disable the haunt, speaks to it in a language other than dwarven, or otherwise takes some action that upsets the spirit.</p><p><strong>Effect</strong> The spirit lashes out in anger, wanting to share its burden. The triggering creature (or the closest creature) must attempt a @Check[will|dc:28|traits:emotion,mental] save.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half of @Damage[(4d8+18)[mental]] damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and begins to sob uncontrollably. It is unable to take reactions for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage and can't use reactions for a minute.</p>"
        },
